# Projects devbrain may plan/execute on. Adding a line here is a deliberate act by
# you, the owner — treat it the same way you'd treat granting write access to a repo.
#
# A repo missing from BOTH this file and devbrain-projects.excluded is not silently
# out of scope — devbrain-repo-audit flags it in the daily digest as unclassified,
# so you notice and make an explicit decision either way.
#
# One repo name per line (must match the directory name under ~/dev/projects/).
# Lines starting with # are comments. This file ships empty except for comments —
# run setup.sh to populate it, or edit it by hand.
#
# Example (remove the leading '#' to enable):
# example-repo
